@startuml Fineract-Project-Setup-and-API-Access-Flow
!include <C4/C4_Context>

title Apache Fineract - Project Setup & API Access Flow Chart

skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor LightBlue
    BorderColor Navy
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BorderColor Orange
}

' Start point
start

' Development Environment Setup
:Development Environment Setup;
note right
**Prerequisites:**
- Java 21+ (OpenJDK/Oracle)
- Gradle 8.x
- MySQL 8.0+ / PostgreSQL 14+
- Git
- IDE (IntelliJ IDEA/Eclipse/VS Code)
end note

:Clone Repository;
note right
**Command:**
git clone https://github.com/apache/fineract.git
cd fineract
end note

:Configure Database;
note right
**MySQL Setup:**
- Create database: fineract_tenants
- Create database: fineract_default
- Update connection properties

**PostgreSQL Setup:**
- Create databases with UTF-8 encoding
- Configure connection pools
end note

:Configure Application Properties;
note right
**Key Configuration Files:**
- application.properties
- application-dev.properties
- gradle.properties

**Database Connection:**
- fineract.tenant.host=localhost
- fineract.tenant.port=3306
- fineract.tenant.username=root
- fineract.tenant.password=mysql
end note

if (Development Mode?) then (yes)
  :Verify Development Prerequisites;
  note right
  **System Requirements:**
  - JDK 21+ (OpenJDK or Oracle JDK)
  - Gradle 8.x+ (or use gradlew wrapper)
  - Git 2.x+
  - IDE with Java support
  - 8GB+ RAM recommended
  - 10GB+ free disk space

  **Database Prerequisites:**
  - MySQL 8.0+ OR PostgreSQL 14+ running
  - Database server accessible on localhost
  - Create databases:
    • fineract_tenants (tenant metadata)
    • fineract_default (default tenant data)
  - Database user with full privileges
  
  **Required Database Setup:**
  MySQL Commands:
  CREATE DATABASE fineract_tenants;
  CREATE DATABASE fineract_default;
  GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON fineract_tenants.* TO 'root'@'localhost';
  GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON fineract_default.* TO 'root'@'localhost';
  FLUSH PRIVILEGES;

  **Environment Configuration:**
  - JAVA_HOME environment variable set
  - Database connection parameters configured
  - Network ports available (8080, 3306/5432)
  - Internet connection for dependency downloads

  **Initial Data Requirements:**
  - Database schemas will be auto-created on first run
  - Sample data loaded via Flyway migrations
  - Default tenant configuration initialized
  - Admin user credentials auto-generated

  **Development Tools (Optional but Recommended):**
  - Postman/Insomnia for API testing
  - Database client (MySQL Workbench/pgAdmin)
  - Git client or IDE integration
  - Docker Desktop (for containerized dependencies)
  end note

  :Build for Development;
  note right
  **Pre-Build Verification:**
  java -version (should show JDK 21+)
  ./gradlew --version (verify Gradle setup)
  mysql -u root -p -e "SHOW DATABASES;" (verify DB connection)
  
  **Clean Build Command:**
  ./gradlew clean build -x test -x rat -x checkstyleMain -x checkstyleTest
  
  **Database Initialization (First Run Only):**
  - Flyway migrations run automatically
  - Creates all required tables and indexes
  - Loads sample data and configurations
  - Sets up default tenant and admin user
  
  **Run Development Server:**
  ./gradlew bootRun --args='--spring.profiles.active=dev'
  
  **Alternative IDE Setup:**
  - Import as Gradle project in IntelliJ/Eclipse
  - Set JDK 21+ as project SDK
  - Configure database connection in application-dev.properties
  - Run FineractPlatformApplication.java main method
  
  **Common Build Issues:**
  - OutOfMemoryError: Increase Gradle heap (-Xmx4g)
  - Database connection failed: Verify MySQL/PostgreSQL running
  - Port 8080 in use: Kill existing processes or change port
  - Missing JDK: Ensure JAVA_HOME points to JDK 21+
  end note
  
  :Access Development Server;
  note right
  **Development URLs:**
  - Main API: http://localhost:8080/fineract-provider
  - Community App: http://localhost:8080/community-app
  - Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/fineract-provider/api-docs/
  - Health Check: http://localhost:8080/fineract-provider/actuator/health
  
  **Verify Server Status:**
  1. Check console logs for "Started FineractPlatformApplication"
  2. Health endpoint returns {"status":"UP"}
  3. Database connections established (check logs)
  4. No error messages in startup sequence
  
  **Default Login Credentials:**
  - Username: mifos
  - Password: password
  - Tenant ID: default
  
  **First-Time Setup Verification:**
  curl -X GET "http://localhost:8080/fineract-provider/api/v1/offices" \
    -H "Authorization: Basic bWlmb3M6cGFzc3dvcmQ=" \
    -H "Fineract-Platform-TenantId: default"
  
  **Development Mode Features:**
  - Hot reload enabled (code changes auto-detected)
  - Debug logging active
  - H2 console available (if configured)
  - Sample data pre-loaded
  - Cross-origin requests enabled
  
  **Troubleshooting Development Issues:**
  - Server won't start: Check database connectivity
  - 404 errors: Verify context path configuration
  - Authentication fails: Check default credentials
  - Slow startup: Increase JVM memory allocation
  - Port conflicts: Change server.port in application-dev.properties
  end note
  
else (no)
  if (Docker Deployment?) then (yes)
    :Docker Setup;
    note right
    **Commands:**
    docker-compose up -d
    
    **Services Started:**
    - fineract-server (Port: 8080)
    - mysql-server (Port: 3306)
    - community-app (Port: 9090)
    end note
    
  else (no)
    :Production Deployment;
    note right
    **Build WAR:**
    ./gradlew clean war
    
    **Deploy to:**
    - Tomcat 9.x+
    - Application Server
    - Cloud Platform (AWS, Azure, GCP)
    end note
  endif
endif

:Server Started Successfully;

' API Access Flow
:API Authentication Setup;

if (Authentication Method?) then (OAuth2)
  :OAuth2 Authentication;
  note right
  **Steps:**
  1. Register OAuth2 Client
  2. Get Client Credentials
  3. Request Access Token
  4. Use Bearer Token in API calls
  
  **Token Endpoint:**
  POST /fineract-provider/api/oauth/token
  end note
  
else (Basic Auth)
  :Basic Authentication;
  note right
  **Default Credentials:**
  - Username: mifos
  - Password: password
  - Tenant: default
  
  **Header:**
  Authorization: Basic bWlmb3M6cGFzc3dvcmQ=
  Fineract-Platform-TenantId: default
  end note
endif

:API Access Methods;

' API Access Options
partition "API Access Options" {
  
  :Web Browser Access;
  note right
  **Community Web App:**
  http://localhost:8080/community-app
  
  **API Documentation:**
  http://localhost:8080/fineract-provider/api-docs/
  
  **Interactive API Testing:**
  Swagger UI interface
  end note
  
  :Mobile Application;
  note right
  **Mobile SDK Integration:**
  - Android Fineract Client
  - iOS Fineract Client
  - React Native
  - Flutter
  
  **API Base URL:**
  https://your-domain.com/fineract-provider/api/v1/
  end note
  
  :API Testing Tools;
  note right
  **Tools:**
  - Postman Collection
  - cURL Commands
  - Insomnia
  - HTTPie
  
  **Sample Request:**
  GET /fineract-provider/api/v1/clients
  Headers:
  - Authorization: Basic [encoded]
  - Fineract-Platform-TenantId: default
  - Content-Type: application/json
  end note
  
  :Direct Integration;
  note right
  **Programming Languages:**
  - Java (Fineract Client)
  - Python (requests library)
  - JavaScript/Node.js (axios)
  - C# (.NET HttpClient)
  - PHP (Guzzle)
  
  **Sample Code:**
  RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();
  HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
  headers.set(Authorization, Basic + encodedCredentials);
  headers.set(Fineract-Platform-TenantId, default);
  end note
}

' API Workflow
:Common API Workflows;

partition "API Operation Flows" {
  
  :Client Management;
  note right
  **Typical Flow:**
  1. POST /clients (Create Client)
  2. GET /clients/{id} (Retrieve Client)
  3. PUT /clients/{id} (Update Client)
  4. POST /clients/{id}?command=activate (Activate)
  
  **Required Data:**
  - firstname, lastname
  - officeId
  - dateFormat, locale
  end note
  
  :Loan Management;
  note right
  **Loan Lifecycle:**
  1. GET /loanproducts (Get Products)
  2. POST /loans (Submit Application)
  3. POST /loans/{id}?command=approve (Approve)
  4. POST /loans/{id}?command=disburse (Disburse)
  5. POST /loans/{id}/transactions (Repayment)
  
  **Accounting Integration:**
  - Automatic journal entries
  - GL account mappings
  end note
  
  :Savings Management;
  note right
  **Savings Flow:**
  1. GET /savingsproducts (Get Products)
  2. POST /savingsaccounts (Create Account)
  3. POST /savingsaccounts/{id}?command=approve
  4. POST /savingsaccounts/{id}?command=activate
  5. POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions (Deposit/Withdrawal)
  end note
  
  :Reporting & Analytics;
  note right
  **Reports Access:**
  1. GET /reports (List Available Reports)
  2. GET /reports/{id} (Generate Report)
  3. GET /runreports/{reportName} (Run Report)
  
  **Data Export:**
  - PDF, Excel, CSV formats
  - Real-time data
  - Scheduled reports
  end note
}

' Error Handling and Monitoring
:Error Handling & Monitoring;

partition "Error Handling" {
  
  :Common API Errors;
  note right
  **HTTP Status Codes:**
  - 400 - Bad Request (Validation errors)
  - 401 - Unauthorized (Authentication failure)
  - 403 - Forbidden (Authorization failure)
  - 404 - Not Found (Resource not found)
  - 500 - Internal Server Error
  
  **Error Response Format:**
  {
    developerMessage: Error details,
    httpStatusCode: 400,
    defaultUserMessage: User-friendly message,
    userMessageGlobalisationCode: error.msg.code,
    errors: [...]
  }
  end note
  
  :Monitoring & Logging;
  note right
  **Monitoring Tools:**
  - Application logs (logback)
  - JMX monitoring
  - Micrometer metrics
  - Custom health checks

  **Log Locations:**
  - logs/fineract.log
  - Database audit tables
  - Transaction logs
  end note
}

' Performance and Security
:Security & Performance;

partition "Security Best Practices" {
  
  :Security Configuration;
  note right
  **Security Measures:**
  - HTTPS/TLS encryption
  - OAuth2 + JWT tokens
  - Multi-tenancy isolation
  - Role-based access control (RBAC)
  - API rate limiting
  - Input validation & sanitization

  **Database Security:**
  - Connection encryption
  - Prepared statements
  - Schema isolation per tenant
  end note
  
  :Performance Optimization;
  note right
  **Performance Tips:**
  - Database connection pooling
  - Query optimization
  - Caching strategies (Redis/Hazelcast)
  - Pagination for large datasets
  - Async processing for heavy operations

  **Scaling Options:**
  - Horizontal scaling (multiple instances)
  - Load balancing
  - Database read replicas
  - CDN for static assets
  end note
}

' Troubleshooting
:Troubleshooting Guide;

partition "Common Issues & Solutions" {
  
  :Startup Issues;
  note right
  **Database Connection Failed:**
  - Check database server status
  - Verify connection properties
  - Ensure database schema exists

  **Port Already in Use:**
  - Change server.port in application.properties
  - Kill existing processes on port 8080

  **Memory Issues:**
  - Increase JVM heap size (-Xmx)
  - Check for memory leaks
  end note
  
  :Runtime Issues;
  note right
  **API Response Slow:**
  - Check database performance
  - Review query execution plans
  - Monitor connection pool

  **Authentication Failures:**
  - Verify credentials
  - Check tenant configuration
  - Review security settings

  **Data Inconsistency:**
  - Check transaction isolation
  - Review concurrent operations
  - Validate data integrity
  end note
}

:Fineract System Ready for Production Use;

stop

note right
Key Success Indicators:
- Server Status: HTTP 200 on /actuator/health
- Database: Connection pool active and responsive
- API Access: Successful authentication and basic operations
- Security: HTTPS configured, proper authentication
- Performance: Response times under acceptable thresholds
- Monitoring: Logging and metrics collection working
- Backup: Database backup strategy implemented
end note

@enduml